🧪 ✅ PART 1: Create VPC + Subnets
🔹 Step 1: Open VPC Dashboard
Login to AWS
In search bar → type VPC → click it
Left side → click Your VPCs
🔹 Step 2: Create VPC
Click Create VPC
Choose VPC only
Enter:
Name: MyVPC
IPv4 CIDR: 10.0.0.0/16
Click Create VPC
🔹 Step 3: Create Subnets
Public Subnet
Left side → Subnets
Click Create subnet
Select your VPC
Name: Public-Subnet
CIDR: 10.0.1.0/24
Click Create
Private Subnet
Click Create subnet
Name: Private-Subnet
CIDR: 10.0.2.0/24
Click Create
🌐 ✅ PART 2: Internet Setup
🔹 Step 4: Create Internet Gateway
Left side → Internet Gateways
Click Create internet gateway
Name: My-IGW
Click Create

👉 Now attach:
5. Click Actions → Attach to VPC
6. Select your VPC → Attach

🔹 Step 5: Route Table for Public Subnet
Left → Route Tables
Click Create route table
Name: Public-RT
Select your VPC → Create
Attach Public Subnet
Select Public-RT
Click Subnet associations tab
Click Edit subnet associations
Select Public-Subnet → Save
Add Internet Route
Go to Routes tab
Click Edit routes → Add route
Enter:
Destination: 0.0.0.0/0
Target: Internet Gateway
Save
💻 ✅ PART 3: Launch EC2 Instances
🔹 Step 6: Launch Bastion Server
Go to EC2 Dashboard
Click Launch instance

Fill:

Name: Bastion-Server
AMI: Ubuntu
Instance type: t2.micro

👉 Key pair:

Click Create new key
Name: bastion.pem
Download it

👉 Network:

VPC: your VPC
Subnet: Public-Subnet
Enable Auto-assign Public IP

👉 Security Group:

Allow SSH (22) → My IP

Click Launch

🔹 Step 7: Launch Database Server
Click Launch instance

Fill:

Name: DB-Server
AMI: Ubuntu

👉 Key pair:

Create: dbserver.pem

👉 Network:

Subnet: Private-Subnet
Auto-assign Public IP: ❌ Disable

👉 Security Group:

Allow:
SSH (22) → Custom → Bastion Private IP
MySQL (3306) → Custom → 10.0.1.0/24

Click Launch

🔑 ✅ PART 4: Connect via Bastion
🔹 Step 8: Connect to Bastion

Open terminal / Git Bash:

ssh -i bastion.pem ubuntu@<BASTION_PUBLIC_IP>
🔹 Step 9: Copy DB Key to Bastion

From your local system:

scp -i bastion.pem dbserver.pem ubuntu@<BASTION_PUBLIC_IP>:/home/ubuntu/
🔹 Step 10: SSH into DB from Bastion

Inside bastion:

ls

Then:
chmod 400 dbserver.pem

ssh -i dbserver.pem ubuntu@10.0.2.x

👉 Now you are inside DB server ✅

❌ Problem (You will face)
sudo apt update

👉 ❌ Will fail (No internet)

🌍 ✅ PART 5: Setup NAT Gateway
🔹 Step 11: Allocate Elastic IP
Go to VPC → Elastic IPs
Click Allocate Elastic IP
Click Allocate
🔹 Step 12: Create NAT Gateway
Left → NAT Gateways
Click Create NAT Gateway

Fill:

Name: My-NAT
Subnet: Public-Subnet
Elastic IP: Select created IP

Click Create

🔁 ✅ PART 6: Private Route Table
🔹 Step 13: Create Route Table
Go to Route Tables
Click Create route table
Name: Private-RT
Select VPC → Create
🔹 Step 14: Attach Private Subnet
Select Private-RT
Subnet associations → Edit
Select Private-Subnet → Save
🔹 Step 15: Add NAT Route
Go to Routes tab
Click Edit routes → Add route

Enter:

Destination: 0.0.0.0/0
Target: NAT Gateway

Click Save

✅ PART 7: Test Internet

Go back to DB server:

sudo apt update

👉 ✅ Now it will work
